1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,900
DEE is an experimental intelligence
technology.

2
00:00:04,015 --> 00:00:09,249
It explores an approach different from
neural-network training: processing through

3
00:00:09,249 --> 00:00:12,390
interactions in a three-dimensional
computational universe.

4
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:16,570
Experience changes relationships that can be
used later.

5
00:00:16,645 --> 00:00:22,530
This is its application: new teaching changes
the response to the same signal.

6
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:31,525
Think of something familiar: we learn an association, remember it, and can revise it
when new information arrives.

7
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:36,200
In DEE, we observe comparable functions through recorded experiments.

8
00:00:36,275 --> 00:00:39,610
Here, the word “clasifica” is used as a signal.

9
00:00:39,685 --> 00:00:42,320
Querying it produces a response.

10
00:00:42,370 --> 00:00:44,820
New teaching is then introduced.

11
00:00:44,895 --> 00:00:48,370
We query the same signal again, and the response changes.

12
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:50,905
Learning means acquiring that relationship.

13
00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:54,030
Memory means retaining it and using it later.

14
00:00:54,090 --> 00:00:58,565
Plasticity means being able to change how the system works through another
experience.

15
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:04,015
The revised response was also observed after saving and reopening the
application.

16
00:01:04,090 --> 00:01:08,685
What had been learned contributed again, without being taught again in that
query.

17
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:16,600
How does this happen inside DEE?

18
00:01:17,070 --> 00:01:19,935
A computer executes DEE’s rules.

19
00:01:19,985 --> 00:01:24,850
Within the model, signals interact and
transform information.

20
00:01:24,925 --> 00:01:30,353
We prepare the conditions for an experience;
encounters change relationships that later

21
00:01:30,353 --> 00:01:32,615
take part in new queries.

22
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:38,840
The rules remain the same, but history changes
how the organization responds.

23
00:01:39,615 --> 00:01:44,410
The points represent elements of the model;
their colors help us follow them.

24
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:47,635
Signals can move and meet.

25
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:54,300
Now let's see how acquired relationships can be combined.

26
00:01:54,450 --> 00:01:59,125
It is similar to using two things already learned to obtain a new response.

27
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:06,655
In this experiment, the experiences establish two relationships: one increases a
value by three, and the other increases it by seven.

28
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:09,955
A new query then arrives with a value of twenty.

29
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:16,695
At the first encounter, the acquired relationship contributes to a transformation
whose interpreted value is twenty-three.

30
00:02:16,880 --> 00:02:20,880
The output continues through space and encounters the second relationship.

31
00:02:20,955 --> 00:02:22,930
The final value is thirty.

32
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:26,205
The sum is a simple way to observe the process.

33
00:02:26,525 --> 00:02:32,900
What matters is that earlier experiences left relationships that contributed to later
encounters.

34
00:02:32,950 --> 00:02:40,960
To establish that contribution, results are compared with controls in which part of
the experience or pathway is removed.

35
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:47,185
This is how composition is studied: one transformation feeds into another within
the same world.

36
00:02:56,250 --> 00:03:00,125
The research also investigates how information can be shared.

37
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:06,075
In communication experiments, a message reached another participant and
affected what it did next.

38
00:03:06,150 --> 00:03:12,280
In transfer experiments, a learned relationship traveled and was used again
elsewhere.

39
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:16,980
The interest lies in preserving its function while changing where it is used.

40
00:03:21,050 --> 00:03:24,675
Remembering also requires access to what has been retained.

41
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:33,945
Alternative pathways were tested: after a new access route was taught, a query
could again use previously acquired content.

42
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:38,370
The information was still there; what changed was how it could be reached.

43
00:03:42,450 --> 00:03:48,725
Predictions made before an outcome, and comparisons with what happens
afterward, have also been tested.

44
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:55,415
In other experiments, consequences changed a reference and altered a later
choice.

45
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:03,150
The analogy is adjusting our response based on what happened: experience
contributes to the next decision.

46
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:11,950
Another capability is bringing different contributions together.

47
00:04:12,025 --> 00:04:21,100
Organizations were built that combined one hundred and twenty-eight input
components, with tests checking each component's contribution.

48
00:04:21,175 --> 00:04:27,975
This makes it possible to investigate how information from multiple sources can be
integrated within a single processing mechanism.

49
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:35,125
These mechanisms have also been studied together.

50
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:46,000
In a trajectory called APD03, the same organization acquired new associations,
retained earlier uses, and used received information to complete tasks.

51
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:56,421
Here we see the course of a recorded task: a request arrives, the required data is
obtained, DEE produces a response, and an external tool generates the

52
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:57,185
corresponding file.

53
00:04:57,260 --> 00:05:04,890
What matters is being able to follow how learning, access to information, and
action contribute to a single history.

54
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:17,355
What has been built brings together a dedicated engine, reusable experimental
mechanisms, and an application for working with them.

55
00:05:17,430 --> 00:05:19,730
DEE Universe is the world's engine.

56
00:05:19,805 --> 00:05:26,735
DEE thinking provides the tools to prepare experiences, observe responses, and
preserve continuity.

57
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:31,990
DEE Cognitive is the application for using the capabilities incorporated into it.

58
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:37,565
This foundation offers resources for research, technical evaluation, and joint
development.

59
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:46,485
It can provide a starting point for assistants with continuity, systems that adjust
their responses, or tools for studying learning.

60
00:05:46,585 --> 00:05:51,910
Each direction draws on mechanisms already investigated and involves its own
development work.

61
00:05:55,983 --> 00:06:04,019
We speak of functional intelligence because of what we observe: acquiring
relationships, remembering, revising responses, combining what has been learned,

62
00:06:04,019 --> 00:06:06,028
and using information to act.

63
00:06:06,128 --> 00:06:12,863
These are functions we associate with intelligent behavior, and DEE makes it
possible to study them through experiments.

64
00:06:12,938 --> 00:06:22,754
The vision is to investigate how organization and experience can give rise to
cognitive capabilities, and explore what principles they might share with natural

65
00:06:22,754 --> 00:06:23,163
processing.

66
00:06:23,238 --> 00:06:30,688
From Puebla, we seek scientific and technological collaboration to develop this
foundation and measure new possibilities.

67
00:06:30,788 --> 00:06:32,683
DEE Cognitive.

68
00:06:32,913 --> 00:06:35,738
Experience changes how the system responds.
